    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Let&#39;s assume I have data on the number of calls each a person placed and the person`s gender.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;d like to visually compare the distributions of call for the two genders in one plot.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The format I&#39;m looking for is a histogram like, but instead of bars I&#39;d like a scatter plot where y is the frequency of the value x (see below).<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">My questions are:<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u><span>1.<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">       </span></span><u></u><span dir=\"LTR\"></span>In my code example (see below) I create a frequency table by manipulating the output of the &quot;table&quot; function. Is there a simpler way to do it?<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u><span>2.<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">       </span></span><u></u><span dir=\"LTR\"></span>How can I create on the same plot the distribution of males &amp; female separately, i.e. a separating them by color.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p><span># Create toy data</span><br><span># x - number of calls</span><br><span># g - gender</span><br><span>df &lt;-</span><span> </span><span>data.frame</span><span>(</span><span>x =</span><span> </span><span>sample</span><span>(</span><span>c</span><span>(</span><span>0</span><span>:</span><span>4</span><span>,</span><span>8</span><span>:</span><span>13</span><span>, </span><span>100</span><span>:</span><span>102</span><span>), </span><span>200</span><span>, </span><span>replace=</span><span>T),</span><br><span>                 </span><span>g =</span><span> </span><span>as.factor</span><span>(</span><span>sample</span><span>(</span><span>c</span><span>(</span><span>&quot;M&quot;</span><span>,</span><span>&quot;F&quot;</span><span>), </span><span>20</span><span>, </span><span>replace=</span><span>T)))</span><br><br><span># Manipulate the data in order to create a &quot;jitter&quot; like histogram</span><br><span>x &lt;-</span><span> </span><span>df$x</span><br><span>tbl &lt;-</span><span> </span><span>table</span><span>(x)</span><br><span>xf &lt;-</span><span> </span><span>as.data.frame</span><span>(tbl)</span><br><span>xf$g =</span><span> </span><span>as.factor</span><span>(</span><span>sample</span><span>(</span><span>c</span><span>(</span><span>&quot;M&quot;</span><span>,</span><span>&quot;F&quot;</span><span>), </span><span>dim</span><span>(xf[</span><span>1</span><span>]), </span><span>replace=</span><span>T))</span><br><span>xf$x &lt;-</span><span> </span><span>as.numeric</span><span>(</span><span>as.character</span><span>((xf$x)))</span><br><br><span># Plot it</span><br><span>ggplot</span><span>(xf,</span><span>aes</span><span>(x,Freq)) +</span><span> </span><span>geom_point</span><span>()</span><u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><img width=\"484\" height=\"388\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/israel-r-user-group/attach/123cfb4b2f5480/image001.png?part=0.0.1&amp;view=1\"><u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Ofrit<u></u><u></u></p></div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<hr style=\"border:none;color:#909090;background-color:#b0b0b0;min-height:1px;width:99%\">\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\t</font></span><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n</font></span><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:none\">\r\n\t<tbody><tr>\r\n\t\t<td style=\"border:none;padding:0px 15px 0px 8px\">\r\n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.avast.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"htt