     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">israel-r-...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">israel-r-...@googlegroups.com</a>] <b>On Behalf Of </b>Michael Dorman<br><b>Sent:</b> Saturday, 1 August 2015 10:05 PM<br><b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">israel-r-...@googlegroups.com</a><br><b>Subject:</b> Re: [Israel RUG] Frequency plot of 2 groups at the with ggplot2<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"># The data</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">df &lt;- data.frame(x = sample(c(0:4,8:13, 100:102), 200, replace=T),<br>                 g = as.factor(sample(c(&quot;M&quot;,&quot;F&quot;), 20, replace=T)))</span><u></u><u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"># Calculating frequency for each combination</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">library(plyr)</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">xf = count(df)</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"># Plot with a different color for each gender</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">library(ggplot2)</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">ggplot(xf,aes(x,freq, colour = g)) + geom_point()</span><u></u><u></u></p></div></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Sat, Aug 1, 2015 at 9:54 AM, Ofrit Lesser &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ofrit....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p><div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Let&#39;s assume I have data on the number of calls each a person placed and the person`s gender.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;d like to visually compare the distributions of call for the two genders in one plot.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The format I&#39;m looking for is a histogram like, but instead of bars I&#39;d like a scatter plot where y is the frequency of the value x (see below).<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">My questions are:<u></u><u></u></p><p>1.<span style=\"font-size:7.0pt\">       </span>In my code example (see below) I create a frequency table by manipulating the output of the &quot;table&quot; function. Is there a simpler way to do it?<u></u><u></u></p><p>2.<span style=\"font-size:7.0pt\">       </span>How can I create on the same plot the distribution of males &amp; female separately, i.e. a separating them by color.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p><p># Create toy data<br># x - number of calls<br># g - gender<br>df &lt;- data.frame(x = sample(c(0:4,8:13, 100:102), 200, replace=T),<br>                 g = as.factor(sample(c(&quot;M&quot;,&quot;F&quot;), 20, replace=T)))<br><br># Manipulate the data in order to create a &quot;jitter&quot; like histogram<br>x &lt;- df$x<br>tbl &lt;- table(x)<br>xf &lt;- as.data.frame(tbl)<br>xf$g = as.factor(sample(c(&quot;M&quot;,&quot;F&quot;), dim(xf[1]), replace=T))<br>xf$x &lt;- as.numeric(as.character((xf$x)))<br><br># Plot it<br>ggplot(xf,aes(x,Freq)) + geom_point()<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><img border=\"0\" width=\"484\" height=\"388\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/israel-r-user-group/attach/12439095e7dfdd/image001.png?part=0.1\"><u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Ofrit<u></u><u></u></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center\"><hr size=\"2\" width=\"99%\" noshade style=\"color:#909090\" align=\"center\"></div><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:0cm 11.25pt 0cm 6.0pt\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"http://www.avast.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.avast.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497255943000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0seLAgL1cHhPktOZO9RYV9\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none\"><img border=\"0\" src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/0Q_vVrbZDtbojQ67yV7xHbpChV0AMQW5PxOF-r8Lnj3VUO7tQeKEoBFYkKeCkgWivYRKezsvSGEvAHd7et2gtKjoJ2kfEg=s0-d-e1-ft#http://static.avast.com/emails/avast-mail-stamp.png\" alt=\"Avast logo\"></span></a><u></u><u></u></p></td><td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"><p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#3d4d5a\">This email has been checked for viruses by Avast antivirus software. <br><a href=\"http://www.avast.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.avast.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497255943000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0seLAgL1